                <pb facs="1028" n="884" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg884"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.7961/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-02-28T19:00:00-05:00">February 28, 1929—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>18. Your 28, February 27, 4 p.m. Department presumes that you have given the
                    formal notice requested by the Minister for Foreign Affairs as well as data
                    about machines and names of pilots.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
